  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compare the variances of the two lotteries and prefer the one with lower variance. However, the individual did not consider variance at all. Instead, they focused on the near-equality of probabilities and the higher monetary payoff in Lottery A. The justification is based on expected value (or a heuristic favoring higher payoff when probabilities are similar), not on risk (variance). Therefore, there is no evidence in the verbal report that the individual used variance as a criterion. The information considered (probabilities and outcomes) is relevant to variance, but the individual did not apply the variance rule. The justification does not align with the variance-based decision rule. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
